.TH Joycond 1 "October 26 2026"

.SH NAME
joycond \- Systemd service to pair joy-cons together into a virtual controller
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B joycond
.RI [ no\-options ]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page documents briefly the
.B joycond
daemon.
.PP
.B joycond
is a
.B Systemd
service that pairs Nintendo Switch joy-cons together into a virtual controller
.SH USAGE
When a joy-con or pro controller is connected via bluetooth or USB, the player LEDs signal that the controller is in pairing mode (by default, LEDs 2 and 4 light up steadily; see CONFIGURATION).

For the pro controller, pressing both triggers will "pair" it.

With the joy-cons, to use a single contoller alone, hold ZL and L at the same time (ZR and R for the right joy-con). Alternatively, hold both S triggers at once.

To combine two joy-cons into a virtual input device, press a *single* trigger on both of them at the same time. A new uinput device will be created called "Nintendo Switch Combined Joy-Cons".

Rumble support is now functional for the combined joy-con uinput device.
.SH CONFIGURATION
joycond reads an optional
.B /etc/joycond.conf
at startup ("key = value" lines; '#' starts a comment).
A missing file means all built-in defaults apply.
Keys:
.TP
.B swap_ab_xy
= true|false (default: false). Swaps the A/B and X/Y buttons
(on paired joy-cons and the pro controller).
Specifically, this remaps:
A (EAST) -> BTN_SOUTH event (keycode 0x130),
B (SOUTH) -> BTN_EAST event (keycode 0x131),
Y (WEST) -> BTN_NORTH event (keycode 0x133), and
X (NORTH) -> BTN_WEST event (keycode 0x134).
.TP
.B thumb_btn_remap_1
= true|false (default: false). A custom remap of the thumbstick click
event to nearby buttons on the paired joy-cons, meant for people who
dislike clicking sticks: MINUS becomes LSTICK, CAP (capture) becomes
MINUS, and HOME becomes RSTICK.
.TP
.B disable_imu
= true|false (default: false). Turns off the IMU (gyro/accelerometer)
on the controllers upon connection, likely saving some power.
.TP
.B rumble_gain
= 0.0-1.0 (default: 1.0). Scales the magnitudes of uploaded rumble
effects before they are forwarded to the physical joy-cons, e.g. 0.5
for half strength.
.TP
.B pair_rumble_mode
= both|left|right|off (default: both). Which physical joy-con(s)
receive forwarded rumble events on the paired (combined) controller.
.SH OPTIONS
.B joycond
has no options
